<article class="env-lemma" id="0CA2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CA2">Lemma <span data-tag="0CA2">55.11.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0C61" data-tag="0C61">55.9.3</a> suppose we have an effective Cartier divisors $D, D' \subset X$ such that $D' = D + C_ i$ for some $i \in \{ 1, \ldots , n\} $ and $D' \subset X_ k$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \chi (X_ k, \mathcal{O}_{D'}) - \chi (X_ k, \mathcal{O}_ D) = \chi (X_ k, \mathcal{O}_ X(-D)|_{C_ i}) = -(D \cdot C_ i) + \chi (C_ i, \mathcal{O}_{C_ i})  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The second equality follows from the definition of the bilinear form $(\  \cdot \  )$ in (<a href="/tag/0C65" data-tag="0C65">55.9.6.1</a>) and Lemma <a href="/tag/0C64" data-tag="0C64">55.9.6</a>. To see the first equality we distinguish two cases. Namely, if $C_ i \not\subset D$, then $D'$ is the scheme theoretic union of $D$ and $C_ i$ (by Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C4R" data-tag="0C4R">31.14.10</a>) and we get a short exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{O}_{D'} \to \mathcal{O}_ D \times \mathcal{O}_{C_ i} \to \mathcal{O}_{D \cap C_ i} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C4J" data-tag="0C4J">29.4.6</a>. Since we also have an exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{O}_ X(-D)|_{C_ i} \to \mathcal{O}_{C_ i} \to \mathcal{O}_{D \cap C_ i} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       (Divisors, Remark <a href="/tag/0C6K" data-tag="0C6K">31.15.11</a>) we conclude that the claim holds by additivity of euler characteristics (Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/08AA" data-tag="08AA">33.33.2</a>). On the other hand, if $C_ i \subset D$ then we get an exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \mathcal{O}_ X(-D)|_{C_ i} \to \mathcal{O}_{D'} \to \mathcal{O}_ D \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C4T" data-tag="0C4T">31.15.3</a> and we immediately see the lemma holds. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>